<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Old Covenant (Iceland)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1262">1262</a>–<a href="/years/1264">1264</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Gamli sáttmáli</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Old Covenant was the agreement of 1262-1264 by which the Icelanders accepted the rule of the Norwegian king Haakon IV and his son Magnus, ending the Icelandic Commonwealth. The chieftains swore allegiance and agreed to pay taxes in return for peace, the keeping of Icelandic law and regular shipping to the island. It followed the civil strife of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sturlung-age">Sturlung Age</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/old-covenant-iceland.jpg" alt="Old Covenant (Iceland)" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Willem Blaeu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1630_IJsland_Blaeu_HR%27.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
